\begin{abstract}
In this paper, we introduce the notion of \CF, which generalizes
\CT s, in order to deal with partially ordered sequences.
We show that algorithms that solve both exact and approximate \CT~Matching
can be adapted to solve \CF~Matching in average linear time.
We adapt the notion of \CT~Signature to \CF s and show 
how filters can be used to experimentally improve the algorithm for the exact matching. 
We also show a one to one correspondence between \CF s and \ST s.
\keywords{\CT ~\and \CF ~\and Pattern Matching \and Approximate Pattern Matching \and \ST}
\end{abstract}


