\section{Multiple Input Switching (MIS)}
\label{sec:SPIC}
In this section, we provide a summary of the MIS effects in CMOS \NOR\
gates % based on FreePDK15$^\text{TM}$ FinFET models~\cite{Nangate15}
reported in~\cite{FMOS22:DATE}. Let $t_A$, $t_B$, and $t_O$ denote the points
in time when the analog trajectories of input signals $A$, $B$, and the output
signal $O$ cross the \emph{discretization threshold voltage} $\vth=\vdd/2$,
respectively. Varying $t_A$ and $t_B$ allows to study the gate delay ($t_O-t_A$
resp.\ $t_O-t_B$, depending on the particular output state) over the relative
\emph{input separation time} $\Delta=t_B-t_A$.

