\subsubsection{Calculating observed proportion}
The observed proportion (see equation \ref{equation:equation3}) represents the percentage of citations which are authored by a specific gender category. It is known as our observed proportion, because it reflects the distribution of gender as it appears among citations in our dataset. %Equation \ref{equation:equation3} expresses the observed proportion for each gender category.
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
&\text{Observed proportion of gender category} \\
&\quad= \frac{\sum \text{(cited papers authored by gender category)}}{\sum \text{(total citations)}} \times 100
\end{aligned}
\label{equation:equation3}
\end{equation}

