\subsubsection{Cluster Creation}
The desired cluster setup is specified in a \texttt{sskuba} configuration file, which has three key sections. 
The \textit{Metadata} section provides the details for creating a unique fully qualified domain name in the target environment. 
The \textit{Target} section specifies the host environment (e.g. AWS, Azure, vSphere), including the number and type of virtual machines to be created. 
Finally, the \textit{GitOps} section provides a reference to a git repository that \texttt{sskuba} uses to bootstrap Flux, whereby \texttt{sskuba} installs the Flux controllers on the cluster and then configures the controllers to synch the cluster state from the specified git repository. 
