The vertices of  Asso$(D_n)$ are in bijection with the 
centrally symmetric \defn{pseudotriangulations} each of which contains exactly $2n$ chords. A \defn{pseudotriangulation} is a partition of a convex polygon into \defn{pseudotriangles}, defined as regions with three convex corners and an arbitrary number of reflex vertices. As in our setting reflex vertices can only come from $O$, pseudotriangles of $P$ contain at most one chain of reflex vertices, and 0,1, or 2 convex vertices on $O$.
The edges of  Asso$(D_n)$ correspond to 
flips of centrally symmetric pairs of chords and the facets correspond to centrally symmetric pairs of (internal) chords. The number of facets, and thus the length of a \fh cycle,  is $n^2$.


