we further explore product constructions of MCs and automata.
Our first main result is a no-go theorem showing
% for coalgebraic product MCs for MCs and NFAs.
% Specifically, we show 
that {\bf \emph{no}} coalgebraic product MCs for MCs and NFAs satisfy the correctness criterion for the model checking problem that asks for the probability of accepting traces (\cref{thm:no-go-mc-nfa}).
To prove this, we characterise natural transformations between certain functors that govern branching types, including non-deterministic and probabilistic branching (\cref{thm:monoid_lambda}). 
