\begin{definition}[semantic structure of the product] \label{def:sem_product}
    The \emph{semantic structure} $(\mathbf{\Omega}_{S\otimes R}, \tau_{S\otimes R})$ is defined by 
    (i) $\mathbf{\Omega}_{S\otimes R} \defeq (\exreal, \leq)$, where $\leq$ is the standard order; and (ii) $\tau_{S\otimes R}\colon \mcnfafunc{\exreal}\rightarrow \exreal$ is given by 
    \begin{align*}
        \tau_{S\otimes R}(\sigma) \defeq \sigma(\checkmark) + \sum_{r\in \exreal} r\cdot \sigma(r). 
