\subsection{Energy Consumption}
\label{energy}
As described in \cite{dualmotes}, the \texttt{dual-motes} employ shunt sensing to detect and amplify the voltage drop across a 0.5 ohm resistor and deduce the electrical \& power consumption in the observed-mote. The observed-mote trigger a GPIO interrupt to trigger the monitor-motes, which subsequently records and relays statistics to a monitor-sink. \textit{It should be noted that the monitor-motes are not participants in the RPL network and rather employ a \texttt{Nullnet} with CSMA CD/CA as a default MAC-layer.} Quite intuitively, one can refer the timestamps from captured packets and the sink as a reference to deduce the electrical/power consumption for corresponding motes. The supply voltage of the dual-motes was set to \texttt{3.3 V} and the resistance of the shunt resistor was \texttt{0.5 Ohms}. Lastly, the amplification factor of the ADC was set to \texttt{51}.
