\begin{definition}[Dual arrangement graph]\label{dualarrangementgrpah}
Given a set $\mathcal{R}$ of connected regions on an oriented surface $\Sigma$.
The dual arrangement graph $G$ has a vertex for each cell of the arrangement, and two vertices are adjacent if and only if the corresponding cells share an arc of the boundary of a region in $\mathcal{R}$, or share a touching point.
