It is easy to see that the dual-arrangement graph is embeddable on the same surface $\Sigma$. 
Since the regions in $\mathcal{R}$ are connected, it follows that for any region $R\in\mathcal{R}$ the subgraph of $G$ induced by cells in $R$, is connected. 
This defines a graph system $(G,\mathcal{R})$ where each region in $\mathcal{R}$ defines a connected subgraph of $G$ induced by the cells contained in it.
