\begin{theorem}
\label{thm:ptastouch}
Let $P$ be a set of points and let $\mathcal{D}$ be a collection of weakly non-piercing regions in the plane.
Then, the following problems admit a PTAS.
\begin{enumerate}
\item The minimum Hitting Set problem for $(P,\mathcal{D})$.
\item The minimum Set Cover problem for $(P,\mathcal{D})$.
\item The maximum Set Packing problem for $(P,\mathcal{D})$ with bounded demands.
\item The maximum Point Packing problem for $(P,\mathcal{D})$ with bounded demands.
\item The minimum dominating set in the intersection graph of the regions $\mathcal{D}$.
\end{enumerate}
