\section*{Limitations}
While we make every effort to ensure that all program pairs in \name{} are correctly labeled, we cannot guarantee complete accuracy. The dataset is constructed using automated transformation pipelines that depend on external toolchains, such as compilers and superoptimizers, which might contain bugs or produce incorrect outputs in edge cases. In addition, some competitive programming submissions used as input source programs may be mislabeled due to incorrect judgments or subtle implementation errors. These sources of noise, though limited in scope, remain a potential source of labeling inaccuracy.


