    Here the tensorized shapes are $M_i = [12, 8, 8]$, $N_i = [8, 8, 12]$, and $R_i = [1, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 1]$.
    Two contraction sequences are visualized as computation graphs. Notably, \textbf{Scheme-2} involves significantly more FLOPs and memory accesses compared to \textbf{Scheme-1}, highlighting the impact of execution sequence on computational efficiency.

