computes the loss across \( N_j \) subtasks, with each subtask requiring \( O(M^2 K) \) time to calculate the SINR terms for \( M \) users, resulting in a total of \( O(N_j \cdot M^2 K) \). The local model update iterates \( N_k \) times, with each parameter update taking constant time \( O(1) \), contributing \( O(N_k) \) to the complexity. When \( L \) is a constant, the overall complexity of the neural network stage is \( O(N_k N_j N_i M^2 K) \), which is significantly lower than traditional methods, with a space complexity of \( O(MK) \).

