\[
\diag(J_{m}(\lambda), -J_{m}(\lambda)^\tp )  Y_{12} + Y_{12} \diag(J_{n}(\mu), -J_{n}(\mu)^\tp ) = 0.
\]
We partition $Y_{12} \in \mathbb{C}^{2m \times 2n}$ as $Y_{12} = \begin{bmatrix}
Z & W \\
U & V
\end{bmatrix}$ where $Z, W, U, V\in \mathbb{C}^{m\times n}$ to obtain 
\begin{align*}
J_{m}(\lambda) Z + Z J_{n}(\mu) &= 0,\quad \ J_{m}(\lambda) W - W J_{n}(\mu)^\tp = 0, \\
-J_{m}(\lambda)^\tp U + U J_{n}(\mu) &= 0,\quad -J_{m}(\lambda)^\tp V - V J_{n}(\mu)^\tp = 0.
\end{align*}

If $\lambda = \mu \ne 0$ then $Z =  V = 0$ and $H_m U, WH_n$ are lower triangular Toeplitz. This implies that $Y_{12}$ has one of the following two forms, depending on $m\ge n$ or $m < n$:
\begin{equation*}
\begin{bsmallmatrix}
0 & 0 \\
0 & T_{\fp} (w_1,\dots, w_{2n}) \\
