\section{Conclusion}
% We propose a novel ego-motion estimation framework that maintains robustness and efficiency in highly dynamic and visually degraded environments. By eliminating reliance on conventional inertial data and complex feature associations, the framework offers a lightweight and adaptable solution well-suited for agile robotic platforms. Extensive experiments validate its capability to provide stable motion estimates in scenarios where traditional methods often fail. The framework is designed as a minimal 6-DoF velocity estimation system, making it a potential alternative to conventional IMU-based approaches.
We propose a robust and efficient ego-motion estimation framework for dynamic, visually challenging environments. It avoids inertial data and complex feature matching, offering a lightweight solution for agile robots. Experiments show stable motion estimates where traditional methods struggle. Designed as a minimal 6-DoF velocity estimator, it can serve as an alternative to IMU-based approaches.
