Another consequence of Theorem~\ref{thmAuT251} is the discovery of a family of vertex-transitive graphs with high $\LS_+$-rank. Given an odd integer $k \geq 3$, the graph $\B_k$ is defined with
\begin{align*}
V(\B_k) \ce{}& \set{ i_0, i_1, i_2, i_3 : i \in [k]},\\
E(\B_k) \ce{}& \set{ \set{i_0, i_1}, \set{i_1, i_2}, \set{i_2, i_3}, \set{i_3, i_0} : i \in [k]} \cup \\
& \set{ \set{i_0,j_2}, \set{i_1,j_3} : (j - i)~\tn{mod}~k \in \set{1,2,\ldots, \frac{k-1}{2}} }.
\end{align*}

