Let $\bI$ be an instance of 
$\Csp(\bS)$. 
A \emph{bijection path in $\bI$ (from $x_0$ to $x_k$)} is a sequence $$x_0,\sigma_1,x_1,\dots,\sigma_k,x_k$$ of elements of $I$ 
such that $(x_{i-1},x_{i}) \in G^{\bI}_{\sigma_i}$ for all $i \in \{1,\dots,k\}$. 

\begin{definition}\label{def:bool-sys}
    The \emph{system of $\mathbb{Z}_2$-linear equations associated to $\bI$} 
    is the $\{L, G_{\id},G_{(01)},R_{\{0\}},R_{\{1\}}\}$-structure
    $\bE$ with domain $I$ and 
    \begin{itemize} 
    \item $L^{\bE} := \Lin^{\bI}$, 
    \item $x_0 \in R^{\bE}_{\{c\}}$, for $c \in \{0,1\}$
    and $x_0 \in I$, 
    if and only if in $\bI$ there exists a bijection 
    path $x_0,\sigma_1,x_1,\dots,\sigma_k,x_k$ 
    %$R_{\sigma_1}(x_0,x_1),R_{\sigma_2}(x_1,x_2)$,
