    \begin{theorem}\label{thm:main}
        For every $n,k \in {\mathbb N}$, the problem 
        $\Csp(\bP^{n,k})$ can be solved by a symmetric linear ${\mathbb Z}_2$-Datalog program with at most $2k^2 + k -2$-many stages.
    \end{theorem}
    \begin{proof} 
    We implement 
    $\Solve_{n,k}$ 
    (Algorithm~\ref{alg:solve}) 
    with a symmetric linear $\mathbb Z_2$-Datalog as follows.
    The special case $k=1$ has already been treated 
    in Proposition~\ref{prop:solven1}. 
